17592186316386} :answer-field/id #uuid "d62400ae-0a5f-5551-b9ba-397f890d3377" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317053}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1dafdbdf-6670-518c-bcd6-eff8e7d1084f" :question/math-academy-id "q-343299" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{3}{x}{y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\\,x>0\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions to the second-order homogeneous differential equation above, where $Q(x)$ is continuous on $(0,\\infty ).$ The Wronskian satisfies $W(2)=5.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\nThe Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies the following first-order differential equation:\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)={{field-1}}W(x)\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we get\n\n$$\nW={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nNow, using the fact that $W(2)=5,$ we obtain \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "The separated calculation below treats $W\\ne0$. The solution $W\\equiv0$ must also be included; allowing $C=0$ in the final formula supplies it.\n\nAbel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{3}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{3}{x}W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-\\frac{3}{x}W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-\\frac{3}{x}\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -\\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{x}^{-3} \\\\ W & =\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(2)=5$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(2) & =\\frac{C}{{2}^{3}} \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{C}{8} \\\\ C & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $W(x)\\ne 0\\text{ for all }x>0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365897 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7fb997a-9a15-5f71-8d90-1aff6caf0292" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)=0$ for some but not all $x>0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365899} {:answer/id #uuid "6b85298d-dbad-5f1d-bc11-7f804b8e1c86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)\\ne 0$ for all $x>0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365900} {:answer/id #uuid "b96999c4-9dfe-5ba0-baf4-01ddfd9be49d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)=0$ for all $x>0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b96999c4-9dfe-5ba0-baf4-01ddfd9be49d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)=0$ for all $x>0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365901} :answer-field/id #uuid "25f2c174-5640-5855-b36a-9241ee95a552" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365898} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3e94415-0b31-57a8-925d-86be8a33581f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C(x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365903} {:answer/id #uuid "6d707dea-4994-5d7a-abc4-7763a91abea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{e}^{-(x+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365904} {:answer/id #uuid "75c50cfa-20f5-55ee-91aa-4cc91e0b6090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365905} {:answer/id #uuid "46b014ba-0349-5dab-986a-3230c4018b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{(x+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75c50cfa-20f5-55ee-91aa-4cc91e0b6090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365905} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0c66c58-9529-5f64-8eae-d3568d6b39ba" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365902} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d32f48fb-9f48-5f8d-aac1-2d9bfae7ddb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365908} {:answer/id #uuid "944aa1bb-2eef-54a1-89ba-4ab67e02b792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{Q(x)}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365909} {:answer/id #uuid "42d3d69c-9157-589f-b9d3-587708493792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365910} {:answer/id #uuid "35fcebaf-a241-54dc-83a1-4a302016a95e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{Q(x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d32f48fb-9f48-5f8d-aac1-2d9bfae7ddb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365908} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd621739-f59b-5606-8972-edb16f5ebfcc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "79e61f49-73ab-5296-adbd-e1c1f22991f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-343292" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{x+1}{y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\\,x>0\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions to the second-order homogeneous differential equation above, where $Q(x)$ is continuous on $(0,\\infty ).$ The Wronskian satisfies $W(1)=0.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies the following first-order differential equation:\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)={{field-1}}W(x)\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we get\n\n$$\nW={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nNow, using the fact that $W(1)=0,$ we obtain \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "The separated calculation below treats $W\\ne0$. The solution $W\\equiv0$ must also be included; allowing $C=0$ in the final formula supplies it.\n\nAbel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{1}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{x+1}W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-\\frac{1}{x+1}W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-\\frac{1}{x+1}\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}(x+1)^{-1} \\\\ W & =\\frac{C}{x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(1)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(1) & =\\frac{C}{1+1} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{C}{2} \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $W(x)=0\\text{ for all }x>0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365912 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88ea0343-23a9-5c1d-b4d2-33f2401611f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3Q(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365914} {:answer/id #uuid "b43f6481-81d9-5e87-8d3b-3a842013d72e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3Q(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365915} {:answer/id #uuid "78e4bcd8-8cda-5a07-87e4-d58c5f1630e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365916} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad2a44f-758a-5e0c-8818-d7f3708c15e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ad2a44f-758a-5e0c-8818-d7f3708c15e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365917} :answer-field/id #uuid "65c6e73a-7d79-5bb4-9b50-c4611ef51ebe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365913} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f58025a8-82af-5015-8ff0-f02604a12a22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365919} {:answer/id #uuid "ed722659-fec2-5798-9b11-d9bad8d0c8ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365920} {:answer/id #uuid "01839665-357f-5e00-9ace-4124db78e520" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365921} {:answer/id #uuid "e4e29dab-0654-5e63-842f-eeb5d8c7fe6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed722659-fec2-5798-9b11-d9bad8d0c8ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365920} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f9fb947-00bb-5fa3-a7f7-918c784a1411" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365918} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b76fa7e6-c148-5fb3-9795-40b4fd671b62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)\\ne 0$ for all $x\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365924} {:answer/id #uuid "fa43b068-1ea7-5914-8563-11d29d4e46fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)=0$ for all $x\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365925} {:answer/id #uuid "4f19d97d-2d5b-5c16-a6c9-765c8be49d3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)=0$ for some but not all $x\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b76fa7e6-c148-5fb3-9795-40b4fd671b62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)\\ne 0$ for all $x\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365924} :answer-field/id #uuid "301928e8-0b57-5f3d-b1ec-39b81b6b7d49" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365923}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2102a071-7b79-557b-964b-dc92d4d14fcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-343306" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions to the second-order homogeneous differential equation above, where $Q(x)$ is continuous on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ The Wronskian satisfies $W(1)=2.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies the following first-order differential equation:\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)={{field-1}}W(x)\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we get\n\n$$\nW={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nNow, using the fact that $W(1)=2,$ we obtain \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "The separated calculation below treats $W\\ne0$. The solution $W\\equiv0$ must also be included; allowing $C=0$ in the final formula supplies it.\n\nAbel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-3W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-3W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-3\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-3x+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{-3x} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(1)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(1) & =C{e}^{-3\\cdot 1} \\\\ 2 & =C{e}^{-3} \\\\ C & =2{e}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $W(x)=2{e}^{3}{e}^{-3x}$ and $W(x)\\ne 0\\text{ for all }x\\in R.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385276 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db2971e6-1fc2-5a15-b561-63195b136074" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385278} {:answer/id #uuid "6b0fa27a-ed94-5c90-a481-896ad99baa7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{Q(x)}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385279} {:answer/id #uuid "7c03e432-04c5-58b2-bf0b-dbaba725fc42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{Q(x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385280} {:answer/id #uuid "63a60a7b-ecc2-5e4a-858a-caf48320bd97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63a60a7b-ecc2-5e4a-858a-caf48320bd97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{{x}^